            <ArticleTitle>[Left atrial myxoma presenting as angor pectoris].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>279-81</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 73 years old woman without cardiovascular risk factors presented physical exercise angina and dyspnea since 8 months ago. The caused of the disease was a left atrial myxoma which entering in left ventricle. The patient was free of coronary injured.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
